      "title": "Course Assistant - Digital Practitioners AI course",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nPart time\n\nJob Description Overview The Part-time Course Assistant provides academic and administrative support for coursework focused on AI, intelligent automation, and their application in real-world business workflows. The role supports faculty and students through grading, exam administration, class support, student communications, and course-related administrative activities. This is a part-time, non-exempt hourly position and does not include teaching responsibilities. Job Responsibilities Grade student papers and examinations. Administer examinations as needed. Attend class lectures and office hours and serve as a Zoom co-host when needed, including monitoring chat during heavily attended sessions. Respond to routine student inquiries regarding course materials and assignment instructions. Escalate complex or in-depth questions regarding course content or assignments to the instructor. Prepare weekly summaries of student inquiries, typically ½ to 1 page. Identify and document course content requiring updates, such as broken links or errors in presentation materials. Perform other administrative duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Ability to apply AI and intelligent automation concepts within real-world business workflows. Understanding of human-in-the-loop and human-on-the-loop approaches to AI and the appropriate use of each. Understanding of automation approaches ranging from basic scripts to agentic systems. Role-specific AI literacy, including building solutions, curating data, integrating workflows, and managing AI-enabled work. Experience working with corporate clients is a plus. Important : Course Assistants may not perform teaching duties. This is not a Teaching Assistant (TA) position. Application Requirements Applicants must submit an updated resume and cover letter. Department WebCampus Student Workers&#xa;&#xa; Compensa