    "https://stevens.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Hoboken-NJ---Main-Campus/Database-Manager-_RQ30627-1": {
      "title": "Database Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nFull time\n\nJob Description This job is for you if you are data-driven, detail-oriented and enjoy working with teams to clean up, maintain and standardize Raiser’s Edge architecture. As a master of queries, imports, merges, and bulk uploads, your work will help maintain a clean and accurate alumni and donor database that enables the team to achieve its communications, engagement, fundraising, and stewardship goals.   The ideal Database Manager is a seasoned leader, including a :   Hands on Raiser's Edge SME who works at the intersection of data, technology, and fundraising strategy—Combining technical rigor with business (Development and Alumni Engagement) understanding.   Technologist/architect who designs the ecosystem and system / platform integrations   Strategist who defines the future of alumni and donor engagement data usage and integrity   Data leader who operationalizes insights, trends, and best practices      Role Overview   The Database Manager is a subject matter expert with 5-7+ years of hands-on experience who administers and manages the Raiser’s Edge constituent management database while maintaining established data entry guidelines and providing support to staff on Raiser’s Edge issues. This role manages all aspects of the Raiser’s Edge database and ensures data cleanliness and integrity, timely donor acknowledgement, and thorough reporting. This position creates, implements and supports systems in Raiser’s Edge that will enable the entire Development and Alumni Engagement Team to perform with greater efficiency and accountability.    This role helps support the end-to-end advancement and alumni data ecosystem, ensuring that technology stack, customer data platforms (CDPs) and integrated technologies enable a unified, data-driven alumni/donor centric experience across fundraising, alumni engagement and communications.   The Database Manager serves as the architect of the alumni and donor data infrastructure, aligning technology, data governance and business strategy to drive established ROI goals, engagement and operational efficiency.    In summary, the position serves as a key strategic partner to Advancement colleagues responsible for fundraising, alumni engagement, donor relations and communications.  By ensuring the accuracy, accessibility and integration of constituent data, the Advancement Database Manager helps drive donor acquisition, retention, stewardship, campaign effectiveness and lifetime alumni engagement.  This role directly supports the university’s ability to build stronger relationships with its alumni and philanthropic community.     Key Responsibilities     - Create queries and exports for complicated lists for multiple internal teams  - Assist with data segmentation queries  - Manage data transfer process into / out of Raiser’s Edge, including multiple other online platforms  - Manage record merging on a weekly basis and keep updated  - Maintain and improve the overall integrity of the Raiser’s Edge database: updating records, merging constituents and adding relevant information provided by donors, prospects or alumni    1. Alumni & Donor Data Strategy   Be part of a team that helps define and execute a multi-year alumni and donor data strategy aligned with university goals   Establish the Blackbaud Raiser’s Edge NXT Database as the single source of truth for alumni, donor and prospect data   Lead development of an alumni and donor 360 model to unify data across systems and touchpoints   Translate business objectives into scalable CRM and data solutions supporting lifecycle alumni and donor engagement   2. Data Governance & Customer Insights   Ensure advanced data quality, integrity, compliance (e.g., privacy, consent) and accessibility   Enable advanced analytics, segmentation and predictive insights using unified customer data   Establish enterprise-wide advanced data governance, taxonomy and standards   Champion data-driven decision-making across teams     3. Integration & Architecture Leadership   Ensure seamless data flow through APIs, middleware and modern integration patterns   Design and oversee database integration architecture across advancement systems (email, alumni engagement, brand, fundraising, reporting, data warehouse, etc.)   Lead initiatives to eliminate data silos and create connected alumni and donor experiences     4. Alumni and Donor Engagement Enablement   Support two key areas across the university:   Alumni Engagement Team – alumni engagement initiatives, activity tracking and list segmentation   Development Team – support annual giving solicitations, prospect pipeline development, relationship tracking, proactive analytics supporting a campaign and major gift solicitation.   Partner with Advancement teams to:    Optimize campaigns, journeys and segmentation   Improve conversion, retention and lifetime value   Enable personalization and lifecycle marketing and engagement through integrated technology platforms   Ensure effective use of Blackbaud Raiser’s Edge NXT Database to deliver targeted, personalized experiences     5. Cross-Functional Leadership   Drive adoption, alignment and standardized processes across functions   Partner with fundraising, donor relations, alumni engagement, corporate relations, communications and IT teams   Lead data governance councils and executive steering committees     6. Operational Excellence & Performance   Define KPIs for CRM and/or database effectiveness (adoption, data quality, pipeline visibility, engagement, ROI)   Optimize workflows, automation and operational processes   Manage teams (indirect reports) including analysts, data engineers, etc.       7. Technology & Platform Ownership   Own the full development and alumni engagement technology stack architecture , including CRM, CDP, automation, analytics, AI and integrations   Evaluate, select and optimize platforms to drive ROI and scalability   Develop and maintain a long-term “Advancement Systems” technology roadmap and ecosystem strategy     8. Core Platforms & Technology Stack   The Advancement Database Manager is expected to have deep, 5-7+ years, expertise across the following categories:   Database Platforms:   Blackbaud Raiser’s Edge NXT   Salesforce Education Cloud or Microsoft Dynamics 365 experience is not required, but bonus points for relevant database experience.     Integrations , Scripting, Reporting, Data Infrastructure, Marketing Automation:   Microsoft Excel   Data warehouses (Snowflake, Redshift, BigQuery)   ETL / ELT pipelines   APIs, Python, middleware / iPaaS   Power BI, Looker, Tableau   GiveCampus, PeopleGrove or Mongoose Cadence experience a plus   Not required, but bonus points for any experience with: Slate, GSC, Google Analytics / Adobe Analytics, customer journey analytics tools, Marketo, Eloqua, Pardot, Journey orchestration platforms    Required Skills & Competencies     Highly detail oriented with an acute degree of accuracy regarding data - ability to navigate data and spreadsheets   Excellent oral and written skills, with the ability to pay close attention to detail   Ability to work well with a team and manage competing priorities   Good organizational, time management, and problem-solving skills and the ability to work accurately and meet deadlines   Ability to work in a flexible way that allows for changes in assignments and priorities   Strong communication and interpersonal skills   Ability to be proactive   Strategic & Executive Leadership   Enterprise CRM, Data Strategy, Tech Stack development   Vendor and platform management   Executive stakeholder influence and cross-functional alignment   Technical & Architectural Expertise   Deep understanding of database architecture and integration patterns, specifically Blackbaud Raiser’s Edge NXT   Data modeling, governance and data lifecycle management   Ability to design scalable, future-proof technology ecosystems   Data & Analytics Fluency Customer segmentation, lifecycle modeling and attribution   Analytics-driven decision making Familiarity with AI/ML applications in user engagement   Operational & Product Mindset Agile product management for database platforms Process automation and optimization Change management and user adoption Core Fundraising and Donor Tech Stack Competencies System-level thinking across data flows and tools Architecture vision and platform selection Tool management and integration planning These competencies are essential to align technology decisions with business outcomes. Experience Requirement 5-7+ years in CRM and/or database management, fundraising technology or customer data leadership roles Proven experience leading enterprise CRM and/or Blackbaud Raiser’s Edge NXT implementations and/or equivalent Experience managing large-scale integrations and data ecosystems Track record of driving measurable and documented growth through CRM and personalization Success Metrics (KPIs) CRM and/or Blackbaud Raiser’s Edge NXT adoption Data quality and completeness Donor and fundraising lifetime value (CLV), retention, engagement, revenue, conversion   Campaign performance and personalization impact Donor and Fundraising ROI     &#xa;&#xa; Department University Advancement Digital Strategy and Engagement&#xa;&#xa; Compensation Range In compliance with the New Jersey Wage Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is $98,000.00 - $133,933.33. This range represents the University’s good faith estimate of possible compensation at the time of posting. Stevens Institute of Technology determines compensation based on factors including the position’s scope and responsibilities, the candidate’s experience, education, skills, internal equity, market data, and organizational considerations. The final salary will be set considering departmental budget, qualifications, and relevant credentials. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes additional forms of compensation, such as incentives, stipends, or other applicable pay components. For a full overview of our benefits offerings, please refer to the Stevens Institute of Technology Benefits Guidebook, available at: Benefits Guidebook &#xa;&#xa; General Submission Guidelines:   Please submit an online application to be considered a candidate for any job at Stevens . Please attach a cover letter and resume with each application. Other requirements for consideration may depend on the job.   Still Have Questions?   If you have any questions regarding your application, please contact Jobs@Stevens.edu .   EEO Statement: Stevens Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Accordingly, Stevens adheres to an employment policy that prohibits discriminatory practices or harassment against candidates or employees based on legally impermissible factor(s) including, but not necessarily limited to, race, color, religion, creed, sex, national origin, nationality, citizenship status, age, ancestry, marital or domestic partnership or civil union status, familial status, affectional or sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, atypical cellular or blood trait, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related medical conditions, disability, or any protected military or veteran status.  Stevens is building a diverse faculty, staff, and student body and strongly encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. Stevens is a federal contractor under the Vietnam Era Veterans' Readjustment Assistance Act (VEVRAA) and the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as well as other federal statutes. Stevens seeks candidates who will contribute to a welcoming and inclusive environment for all students, faculty and staff. Jeanne Clery Disclosure:  In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act), the Department of Public Safety is required to publish an annual security report which includes statistics mandated by the Clery Act. Click here for a copy of this report."
    },
    "https://stevens.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Hoboken-NJ---Main-Campus/Assistant-Club-Ice-Hockey-Team-Coach_RQ30867-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Club Ice Hockey Team Coach",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nPart time\n\nJob Description Stevens Institute of Technology invites applications for the part-time position of Assistant Club Ice Hockey Coach. Stevens Campus Recreation offers 14 club sports, a wide variety of intramural sports and special events, an extensive outdoor adventure program, and a wide selection of wellness/fitness classes. Located in Hoboken, New Jersey, a historic small town just minutes away from Manhattan, Stevens has an enrollment of over 4,100 undergraduate students. This position oversees the growth and development of club ice hockey student-athletes. The position is responsible for communicating departmental and team rules and educating the students regarding policies and procedures outlined in the club sports handbook. Essential Responsibilities: Assist head coach with managing all aspects of a competitive Club Ice Hockey program. Plan and attend all team practices home and away contests. Assist with organizing the team’s schedule and coordinating team travel. Work together to ensure a positive and collaborative team environment for all club members. Additional duties to be determined by the Director of Campus Recreation. Qualifications: Education     Bachelor’s degree required. Experience     Previous coaching experience at the collegiate level is strongly preferred. Specialized Licenses     First Aid, CPR, AED training certification required or obtained upon employment. Specific Skills:     Must be willing to work evenings, weekends, and holidays. Department Club Sports&#xa;&#xa; Compensation Range In compliance with the New Jersey Wage Transparency Act, the hourly base range for this position is $16.00-$16.00/ an hour. This range represents the University’s good faith estimate of possible compensation at the time of posting. Stevens Institute of Technology determines compensation based on factors including the position’s scope and responsibilities, the candidate’s experience, education, skills, internal equity, market data, and organizational considerations. The final salary will be set considering departmental budget, qualifications, and relevant credentials. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes additional forms of compensation, such as incentives, stipends, or other applicable pay components. For a full overview of our benefits offerings, please refer to the Stevens Institute of Technology Benefits Guidebook, available at: Benefits Guidebook &#xa;&#xa; General Submission Guidelines:   Please submit an online application to be considered a candidate for any job at Stevens . Please attach a cover letter and resume with each application. Other requirements for consideration may depend on the job.   Still Have Questions?   If you have any questions regarding your application, please contact Jobs@Stevens.edu .   EEO Statement: Stevens Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Accordingly, Stevens adheres to an employment policy that prohibits discriminatory practices or harassment against candidates or employees based on legally impermissible factor(s) including, but not necessarily limited to, race, color, religion, creed, sex, national origin, nationality, citizenship status, age, ancestry, marital or domestic partnership or civil union status, familial status, affectional or sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, atypical cellular or blood trait, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related medical conditions, disability, or any protected military or veteran status.  Stevens is building a diverse faculty, staff, and student body and strongly encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. Stevens is a federal contractor under the Vietnam Era Veterans' Readjustment Assistance Act (VEVRAA) and the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as well as other federal statutes. Stevens seeks candidates who will contribute to a welcoming and inclusive environment for all students, faculty and staff. Jeanne Clery Disclosure: