    "https://stevens.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Hoboken-NJ---Main-Campus/Postdoctoral-Data-Driven-Organizational-Skill-Networks_RQ30950-1": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral-Data-Driven Organizational Skill Networks",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-27\nPart time\n\nJob Description The proposed PosDoc position will support the project Data-Driven Organizational Skill Networks: Developing a Master Skill Map for Workforce Capability and Gap Analysis. The individual will conduct research involving natural language processing (NLP), artificial intelligence (AI), machine learning, and network analytics to identify, extract, normalize, and analyze workforce skills from heterogeneous organizational datasets. Responsibilities will include developing computational methods for constructing organizational skill networks, integrating these networks into a Master Skill Map, and designing quantitative metrics to assess skill coverage, organizational strengths, emerging capabilities, and workforce skill gaps. The researcher will also contribute to data collection and validation, comparative organizational analyses, interactive visualizations, technical documentation, research reports, and scholarly publications. The position requires strong analytical and programming skills, particularly in Python, along with familiarity with data science, network analysis, and computational research methodologies. Department Enterprise Science and Engineering&#xa;&#xa; Compensation Range In compliance with the New Jersey Wage Transparency Act, the annual base range for this position is $60,000. This range represents the University’s good faith estimate of possible compensation at the time of posting. Stevens Institute of Technology determines compensation based on factors including the position’s scope and responsibilities, the candidate’s experience, education, skills, internal equity, market data, and organizational considerations. The final salary will be set considering departmental budget, qualifications, and relevant credentials. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes additional forms of compensation, such as incentives, stipends, or other applicable pay components. For a full overvie