      "title": "Course Developer - CPE",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nPart time\n\nJob Description Under the direction of CPE instructional designers, develop the next version of the Hartford cohort for Enterprise AI for SWE and Enterprise AI for DS. - Manage syllabus materials - Provide course content and subject materials to the course designers - Review materials for content and accuracy. This is a part-time position. Education: Bachelor, Master or Ph.D.in area of experience.  Department Online Adjuncts&#xa;&#xa; Compensation Range In compliance with the New Jersey Wage Transparency Act, the base salary range for this position is listed below. This range represents the University’s good faith estimate of possible compensation at the time of posting. Stevens Institute of Technology determines compensation based on factors including the position’s scope and responsibilities, the candidate’s experience, education, skills, internal equity, market data, and organizational considerations. The final salary will be set considering departmental budget, qualifications, and relevant credentials. &#xa; < 8 Students: $1,000/student 8-16 Students: $8,025 17-25 Students: $9,150 26-50 Students: $10,300 &#xa; General Submission Guidelines:   Please submit an online application to be considered a candidate for any job at Stevens . Please attach a cover letter and resume with each application. Other requirements for consideration may depend on the job.     Academic Submission Guidelines:     Please submit :     Cover letter   C urriculum vitae   R esearch statement T eaching statement that includes a) teaching interests, b) teaching philosophy, and c) a plan on how to create an inclusive environment for students of all backgrounds in terms of classroom teaching, student advising, and graduate student mentoring   C ontact info for at least 2-3 references ( school-specific ; p lease refer to job posting )     Still Have Questions?   If you have any questions regarding your application, please contact Jobs@Stevens.edu .   EEO Statement: Stevens Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Accordingly, Stevens adheres to an employment policy that prohibits discriminatory practices or harassment against candidates or employees based on legally impermissible factor(s) including, but not necessarily limited to, race, color, religion, creed, sex, national origin, nationality, citizenship status, age, ancestry, marital or domestic partnership or civil union status, familial status, affectional or sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, atypical cellular or blood trait, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related medical conditions, disability, or any protected military or veteran status.  Stevens is building a diverse faculty, staff, and student body and strongly encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. Stevens is a federal contractor under the Vietnam Era Veterans' Readjustment Assistance Act (VEVRAA) and the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as well as other federal statutes. Stevens seeks candidates who will contribute to a welcoming and inclusive environment for all students, faculty and staff. Jeanne Clery Disclosure:  In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act), the Department of Public Safety is required to publish an annual security report which includes statistics mandated by the Clery Act. Click here for a copy of this report."
    },
    "https://stevens.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Hoboken-NJ---Main-Campus/Research-Scientist---Postdoctoral-Researcher-in-Cyber-Physical-Systems--Trustworthy-AI_RQ30929-2": {
      "title": "Research Scientist / Postdoctoral Researcher in Cyber-Physical Systems, Trustworthy AI",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nFull time\n\nJob Description Responsibilities •              Lead day-to-day project execution. Develop and maintain research plans, milestones, responsibilities, and deliverable schedules. Track progress, identify risks and dependencies, and initiate follow-up and corrective actions. •              Mentor graduate and undergraduate researchers. Hold regular technical meetings, help students define achievable objectives, review their work, troubleshoot obstacles, and develop their independence and research judgment. •              Coordinate with program managers and collaborators. Prepare technical updates, organize meetings, communicate results and challenges clearly, and follow through on agreed actions in coordination with the PI. •              Conduct and guide substantive research. Contribute original methods, software, experiments, or system implementations in relevant research areas and help ensure the technical quality of the team’s work. •              Lead preparation of research outputs. Coordinate and contribute to manuscripts, sponsor reports, presentations, demonstrations, and other project deliverables. •              Strengthen research practices. Support reproducible experiments, clear documentation, shared code and data practices, and effective onboarding of new researchers. •              Contribute to proposal development and identify opportunities for collaboration and future research.   Required qualifications •              A Ph.D. in computer science, electrical or computer engineering, systems engineering, or a closely related field by the start date. •              A strong research record in at least one area relevant to the group. •              Demonstrated experience coordinating research activities, leading a technical project or workstream, or mentoring junior researchers. •              Ability to translate broad research objectives into concrete tasks, realistic timelines, and measurable outcomes. •              Strong technical writing, presentation, and interpersonal communication skills. •              Evidence of initiative, sound judgment, reliable follow-through, and the ability to manage multiple priorities. •              A collaborative and supportive mentoring approach, with a commitment to research rigor and student development.   Preferred qualifications •              Experience working on externally funded, milestone-driven, or multi-institution research projects. •              Experience communicating with government program managers, industry partners, or other external stakeholders. •              Experience guiding student work toward publications, working prototypes, or research demonstrations. •              Hands-on experience with relevant software, hardware, simulation environments, or experimental testbeds. •              Experience contributing to proposals and technical reports.   Appointment and professional development Appointment title and scope will be determined based on experience and institutional requirements. Candidates for the Research Scientist role should demonstrate sustained independent research and team leadership. Postdoctoral candidates should demonstrate readiness to assume responsibility for a defined research effort and mentor junior researchers.   The position offers opportunities to publish, develop an independent research direction aligned with the group’s programs, build collaborations, and gain experience in research leadership and proposal development. We offer competitive compensation commensurate with qualifications and experience.     Application materials Interested applicants should submit: •              A curriculum vitae, including publications. •              A brief cover letter describing relevant research expertise and interest in the role. •              Contact information for three references who can comment on research ability, leadership, mentoring, and reliability.   For inquiries, contact Professor Ying Wang at ywang6@stevens.edu , using the subject line “Research Scientist / Postdoctoral Researcher Inquiry.”     Department Wireless Communications and Health AI&#xa;&#xa; Compensation Range In compliance with the New Jersey Wage Transparency Act, the annual base range for this position is $80,000-$110,000. This range represents the University’s good faith estimate of possible compensation at the time of posting. Stevens Institute of Technology determines compensation based on factors including the position’s scope and responsibilities, the candidate’s experience, education, skills, internal equity, market data, and organizational considerations. The final salary will be set considering departmental budget, qualifications, and relevant credentials. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes additional forms of compensation, such as incentives, stipends, or other applicable pay components. For a full overview of our benefits offerings, please refer to the Stevens Institute of Technology Benefits Guidebook, available at: Benefits Guidebook &#xa;&#xa; General Submission Guidelines:   Please submit an online application to be considered a candidate for any job at Stevens . Please attach a cover letter and resume with each application. Other requirements for consideration may depend on the job.   Still Have Questions?   If you have any questions regarding your application, please contact Jobs@Stevens.edu .   EEO Statement: Stevens Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Accordingly, Stevens adheres to an employment policy that prohibits discriminatory practices or harassment against candidates or employees based on legally impermissible factor(s) including, but not necessarily limited to, race, color, religion, creed, sex, national origin, nationality, citizenship status, age, ancestry, marital or domestic partnership or civil union status, familial status, affectional or sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, atypical cellular or blood trait, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related medical conditions, disability, or any protected military or veteran status.  Stevens is building a diverse faculty, staff, and student body and strongly encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. Stevens is a federal contractor under the Vietnam Era Veterans' Readjustment Assistance Act (VEVRAA) and the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as well as other federal statutes. Stevens seeks candidates who will contribute to a welcoming and inclusive environment for all students, faculty and staff. Jeanne Clery Disclosure:  In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act), the Department of Public Safety is required to publish an annual security report which includes statistics mandated by the Clery Act. Click here for a copy of this report."
    },
    "https://stevens.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Hoboken-NJ---Main-Campus/Coordinator--Schaefer-School-of-Engineering-and-Science_RQ30862": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Schaefer School of Engineering and Science",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nPart time\n\nJob Description Working under the supervision of the Associate Director of Undergraduate Studies, the Coordinator provides administrative and office support to the Schaefer School’s Office of the Dean, Undergraduate Studies.   This is a part-time, fixed-term, hybrid position. Must have the ability to work weekdays (Wednesday and Friday availability preferred) from 9 a.m.-2 p.m., with off hours and weekends, as needed.   Essential Duties and Responsibilities Provide administrative and logistical support for meetings, events, and committees (Dean’s Undergraduate Student Advisory Council (DUSAC), the SES Undergraduate Curriculum Committee (UGCC), Order of the Engineer ceremony, etc.) including, but not limited to: Scheduling meeting/conference space(s) Preparing, managing, and distributing meeting agendas and minutes Coordinating catering/supply delivery logistics. Maintain certificate and award templates and process award checks for special academic events and competitions, including: Ansary Entrepreneurship Competition Gallois Autonomous Robot Competition Several endowed Senior Design awards Coordinate job posting and onboarding of Adjunct Instructors, Teaching Assistants (TA), Lab Assistants (LA), and Course Assistants (CA) in Engineering Core courses. Assist with Workday and Coursedog logistics regarding course section scheduling and instructor assignments. Coordinate with the Associate Director and Schaefer School departments to ensure accurate TA, LA, and CA budgeting, time allocation, and payroll. Maintain access information to facilities for Graduate and Teaching Assistants and Lab Monitors. Perform other related duties, as needed.   Qualifications Required Education:  High School Diploma Preferred Education:  Bachelor’s degree or equivalent combination of education and experience. Required Experience:  1 year of experience in an office setting Preferred Experience:  1 year of experience in higher education   Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities  A self-starter who demonstrates an ability to achieve goals and meet deadlines. A high level of professionalism with strong interpersonal and organizational skills. Ability to manage multiple tasks and projects with high attention to detail in a fast-paced environment. Advanced understanding of the Microsoft Office suite, with particular proficiency in Word, Outlook, Excel, Teams, and PowerPoint. Proficiency in virtual meeting platforms such as Zoom or MS Teams. Possess excellent organizational, written, oral communication, and presentation skills  Skills in designing graphics for fliers and marketing using Canva and other applications, preferred. Willingness to occasionally work evenings and weekendsExempt (Salary) Department SES Core Engineering&#xa;&#xa; Compensation Range In compliance with the New Jersey Wage Transparency Act, the hourly base range for this position is $25 - $28. This range represents the University’s good faith estimate of possible compensation at the time of posting. Stevens Institute of Technology determines compensation based on factors including the position’s scope and responsibilities, the candidate’s experience, education, skills, internal equity, market data, and organizational considerations. The final salary will be set considering departmental budget, qualifications, and relevant credentials. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes additional forms of compensation, such as incentives, stipends, or other applicable pay components. For a full overview of our benefits offerings, please refer to the Stevens Institute of Technology Benefits Guidebook, available at: Benefits Guidebook &#xa;&#xa; General Submission Guidelines:   Please submit an online application to be considered a candidate for any job at Stevens . Please attach a cover letter and resume with each application. Other requirements for consideration may depend on the job.   Still Have Questions?   If you have any questions regarding your application, please contact Jobs@Stevens.edu .   EEO Statement: Stevens Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Accordingly, Stevens adheres to an employment policy that prohibits discriminatory practices or harassment against candidates or employees based on legally impermissible factor(s) including, but not necessarily limited to, race, color, religion, creed, sex, national origin, nationality, citizenship status, age, ancestry, marital or domestic partnership or civil union status, familial status, affectional or sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, atypical cellular or blood trait, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related medical conditions, disability, or any protected military or veteran status.  Stevens is building a diverse faculty, staff, and student body and strongly encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. Stevens is a federal contractor under the Vietnam Era Veterans' Readjustment Assistance Act (VEVRAA) and the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as well as other federal statutes. Stevens seeks candidates who will contribute to a welcoming and inclusive environment for all students, faculty and staff. Jeanne Clery Disclosure:  In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act), the Department of Public Safety is required to publish an annual security report which includes statistics mandated by the Clery Act. Click here for a copy of this report."
